---
description: Auth and security invariants for this project
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security

- Session tokens live in `HttpOnly` cookies only. Never `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
- Access JWT is short-lived; refresh tokens are stored hashed and rotated.
- Sign-in errors are generic. Do not reveal whether an email exists.
- Validate every input on the server. Shared Zod schemas are the source of truth.
- Email uniqueness is a Mongo unique index, not only an application check.
- Never log passwords, cookies, Authorization headers, or token values.
- Never return `passwordHash`. Hash passwords with argon2id.
- `Secure` cookies in production. `SameSite=Lax`. Same-origin `/api` proxy.
